    <string name="terms_main_title">Terms &amp; Conditions of Use - Gradia</string>
    <string name="terms_last_updated">Last updated: May 2026</string>

    <string name="terms_section1_title">1. Acceptance of Terms</string>
    <string name="terms_section1_body">By downloading, installing, or using the Gradia application, you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree with any of the terms set forth herein, please do not use the application.</string>

    <string name="terms_section2_title">2. Description of Service</string>
    <string name="terms_section2_body">Gradia is a mobile application designed for university students to keep track of their grades, subjects per semester, academic goals, and personal progress. The app is an academic support tool and has no official affiliation with educational institutions.</string>

    <string name="terms_section3_title">3. Registration and User Account</string>
    <string name="terms_section3_body">You are responsible for providing truthful information when registering. You must maintain the confidentiality of your access credentials. Gradia is not responsible for unauthorized access resulting from misuse of your password. You may delete your account at any time from the application settings.</string>

    <string name="terms_section4_title">4. Acceptable Use</string>
    <string name="terms_section4_body">You agree to use Gradia solely for personal and academic purposes. The following is prohibited: Attempting to access other users\' data. Using the application for commercial purposes without express authorization. Reverse engineering, decompiling, or modifying the application.</string>

    <string name="terms_section5_title">5. Privacy and Data Handling</string>
    <string name="terms_section5_body">The academic data you enter (grades, subjects, goals) is stored locally on your device and, if you use cloud synchronization, on protected servers. We do not sell or share your personal academic information with third parties. We may collect anonymous usage data to improve the app experience. For more details, see our Privacy Policy.</string>

    <string name="terms_section6_title">6. Intellectual Property</string>
    <string name="terms_section6_body">All elements of Gradia — including design, icons, name, logo, and code — are the property of its developers and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws. Total or partial reproduction without authorization is prohibited.</string>

    <string name="terms_section7_title">7. Limitation of Liability</string>
    <string name="terms_section7_body">Gradia is provided \"as is.\" The developers do not guarantee that the application is error-free or that it will function uninterrupted. In no event shall we be liable for loss of academic data, decisions made based on information displayed in the app, or indirect damages resulting from its use.</string>

    <string name="terms_section8_title">8. Modifications</string>
    <string name="terms_section8_body">We reserve the right to update these Terms and Conditions at any time. We will notify you of important changes through the application. Continued use of Gradia after an update implies acceptance of the new terms.</string>

    <string name="terms_section9_title">9. Contact</string>
    <string name="terms_section9_body">If you have questions about these Terms and Conditions, you can contact us through the support section within the application or write to us at soporte@gradia.app.</string>

